# Product Rules

## What this is

This folder uses [cursor-rules-rea](https://github.com/BOXELS/cursor-rules-rea) — the Cursor rules template for official [REA](https://github.com/morluto/rea). Same idea as cursor-rules: copy it in, and the AI already knows the workflow. There is no second template.

## Who uses this

Primary user: someone who can name software they are allowed to inspect and say what they want to understand. They may not be a coder. Do not ask them to use another GitHub repo.

## Key user flows

1. Copy or "Use this template" → open in Cursor → `/start-investigation` → authorize → inspect → findings
2. Follow one feature through evidence → explain it → optionally reconstruct it
3. If REA is missing, run official setup once, restart Cursor, continue

Every new task should connect to one of these flows.

## Current investigation

- Target name: [fill with /setup-investigation]
- Authorization: [own / written permission / N/A — not started]
- Artifact path: [absolute path or installed app]
- Primary question: [what we want to understand]
- Out of scope: DRM, anti-cheat, license bypass, unauthorized services, exploit development

## Tone of voice

Plain language first. Do not dump git or npx unless a missing tool needs one command.

## Legal and compliance

See `docs/AUTHORIZATION.md` and [REA's disclaimer](https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/DISCLAIMER.md). Do not proceed without a stated authorization basis.
